The first expanded v2 audit draft is preserved as `i03-var08-independent-contract-audit-v2-failed-null-draft.py`, SHA-256 `426f538e13987b74a944b87522abdba363303e2f2550e73b9837d4bffd32617f`.

Its first execution returned OS exit 1 and a decoded tool transcript ending at `source_and_custody`, line 116, `assert numeric_equal(a, b)`, `AssertionError`. The draft treated every declared-double source/export cell as numeric; optional null cells are valid and require exact null equality. The original command stdout/stderr byte streams were not separately captured, so this note does not claim byte custody of those streams. No native command or accepted checker was invoked.
